WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.960
Every fall, many monarch butterflies fly south through Virginia.

2
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.840
Every spring, cherry trees in Washington, D.C., burst into bloom.

3
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.200
A butterfly has no calendar.

4
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.160
A tree has no eyes.

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.580
So how do plants and animals know when to sleep, bloom, or fly south?

6
00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:22.823
Start with one day.

7
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:27.963
A circadian rhythm is a pattern that repeats about every 24 hours.

8
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:31.283
Light and darkness help keep it in step with the day.

9
00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:34.383
Many owls hunt at night and rest in the day.

10
00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:36.423
Tree squirrels do the opposite.

11
00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:41.103
In many animals, the rhythm keeps going for a while in steady darkness.

12
00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:44.483
So part of the timing comes from inside the body.

13
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.843
Plants respond too, often by growing.

14
00:00:48.803 --> 00:00:51.683
A tropism is plant growth toward or away from something.

15
00:00:52.703 --> 00:00:53.803
Light shines from one side.

16
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:58.763
Cells on the shaded side of the stem grow longer than cells on the lit side.

17
00:00:59.623 --> 00:01:02.723
The longer side pushes the stem into a bend toward the light.

18
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:07.017
Now think about a Virginia winter.

19
00:01:08.177 --> 00:01:11.417
Days are short, nights are cold, and many foods are hard to find.

20
00:01:12.397 --> 00:01:15.117
Cues like day length and temperature help time the responses.

21
00:01:16.277 --> 00:01:17.697
Monarchs migrate south in fall.

22
00:01:18.997 --> 00:01:23.497
Migration is the seasonal movement of animals from one region to another and back.

23
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.997
Dormancy is a resting state.

24
00:01:26.977 --> 00:01:29.857
Growth slows or stops, but the living thing stays alive.

25
00:01:30.897 --> 00:01:32.857
Hibernation is dormancy in animals.

26
00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:37.137
A groundhog's body temperature drops, so it uses less stored fat.

27
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.710
Are these behaviors learned?

28
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.910
For monarchs, mostly not.

29
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.950
An instinct is a behavior an animal inherits and can do without being taught.

30
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.570
A monarch flying south has never made the trip before.

31
00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:52.913
So how do they know?

32
00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:57.113
They respond to cues, such as light, day length, and temperature.

33
00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:01.353
In animals, many of these responses are inherited instincts.

34
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:05.213
Some changes last for many years, like a warming climate.

35
00:02:06.153 --> 00:02:08.233
Those can shift when these responses happen.
